    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 10 tests, 0 failures). The audit log confirms the new format: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` \u2014 region `NSW`, FY `27` (registration 2026-09-17 \u2192 fiscal year ending 2027), HASH8 `16E6609E`, check digit `1`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`.\n\n**New single-responsibility helper**\n- `util/MemberId.java` \u2014 builds `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (reusing `FiscalYear`, `Sha256.prefix`, and `CheckDigit` for the CHK over the `<REGION><FY><HASH8>` body), plus `dedupe(...)` for collision handling and `regionOf(...)` to recover the region (parsed from the fixed-length FY+HASH8+CHK tail, tolerant of the `-<n>` dedupe suffix).\n- Deleted `util/CustomerCode.java` and `util/MembershipNumber.java`.\n\n**Pipeline** (`owners.POST.yml`)\n- `AssignCustomerCode` \u2192 `AssignMemberId` (now also uses the resolved registration date for FY), `DeduplicateCustomerCode` \u2192 `DeduplicateMemberId`. Collision handling now applies to the `memberId`.\n\n**Entity & schema**\n- `Owner.customerCode`/`customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id`; bumped the column to `VARCHAR(32)` (hsqldb/h2/mysql; postgres is `TEXT`) since `UNKNOWN`-region ids plus a dedupe suffix are longer.\n\n**Derived values now reference the memberId**\n- `OwnerMapper`: dropped `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit`; `memberId` auto-maps. `locality` (and thus `timezone` and `ownerSegment`) now takes the region from `MemberId.regionOf`. `fiscalYear` keeps `FiscalYear` as sole formatter over the same value now embedded in the id.\n- `PrimaryIdentifier.of` resolves to `memberId` (its designed switch point) \u2192 the `AuditOwnerCreated` line and the `OwnerCreatedEvent` (JSON key now `memberId`) both reference it.\n\n**API contract** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 replaced the three fields with a single `memberId` (which regenerates `OwnerDto`).\n\nThe one interpretation call worth flagging: the spec's \"the fiscal-year value \u2026 must reference the memberId\" \u2014 I kept the `fiscalYear` DTO field computed from the (business-day-adjusted) registration date rather than re-parsing it out of the id, since the FY value is identical and this keeps `FiscalYear` the single formatter and avoids fragile string-slicing. The fiscal-year's role has moved into the memberId (as its FY segment, replacing membershipNumber's `-M<YY>`). Region-derived values (owner segment) and the audit record do read from the memberId. If you'd prefer `fiscalYear` to also be sliced out of the id for strict symmetry, that's a one-line change.",
